Refactor the component so the selection update has one named handler and the values derived from selectedIds stay as render-time calculations:

```tsx
const selectedCount = selectedIds.length;
const hasSelection = selectedCount > 0;

const handleSelectionToggle = (id: string) => {
  setSelectedIds((previousSelectedIds) =>
    previousSelectedIds.includes(id)
      ? previousSelectedIds.filter((selectedId) => selectedId !== id)
      : [...previousSelectedIds, id],
  );
};
```

Remove the separate count/flag state and the effect that synchronizes them from selectedIds. Place selectedCount and hasSelection next to the render logic that consumes them, and replace the inline toggle with a call such as `handleSelectionToggle(id)`. Leave the existing navigation callbacks, route behavior, class names, and style props untouched.
